Subject: [PATCH 278/398] Unified: the parts shelf panel, "Insert screw" for a
 picked hole, profiles by two clicks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PartsShelfGui.py: the commands Unified_PartsShelf (tool strip, Ctrl+K), Unified_InsertScrew
(the bar next to a picked hole) and Unified_PlaceProfile. The panel lists the screws, nuts and
washers (JIS names), the profiles and the company parts, with a search ("M6×20", "ナット").
Clicking a hole puts the screw that fits it; the size, length, washers, nut and an extra plate
can be changed and redo the last one. A profile goes from one click to the next (a ghost
follows the cursor; or type the length), a company part onto the clicked face.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
